;; aratame — bundled indicator seed.
;;
;; This file dates itself, and the default policy floor is 7 days. That is not
;; an oversight: a bundled list with no expiry is exactly how a product ends up
;; asserting "clean" from a list nobody has updated since the release. A week
;; after this file was written, every verdict computed against it alone becomes
;; :unmeasured until an operator points aratame at a current feed.
;;
;; The one entry is the EICAR standard anti-malware test file — a published,
;; deliberately harmless 68-byte string that exists so a detection path can be
;; exercised end to end without handling a real sample. Its hashes were computed
;; from the string itself, not copied from a page.
